
Wassup, everyone, it’s me, MesterKNGT, and welcome back to another thrilling post on the FNF_Thoughts repo!
Today, we’re gonna be talking about where it all began, how FNF became what it is today
You’re probably wondering, how did FNF get its start, where did it originate from?
If you said the itch.io prototype, you’re partly correct, as that was where it was first found, but where did it form from>
You see, the game is supposed to a love letter to the amazing platform of Newgrounds, as many die-hard Funkheads know
What is Newgrounds, you ask, well, let me answer that question of yours

About 33-34 years from now, an ordinary guy wanted to create an independently published magazine service that could 
keep you up to speed on all things video games related
He got around to making a website for it later, in the 1995, but this website was actually used for user-submissions
This man, as you might assume, is the top dawg Tom Fulp, who has a penis but we’re not sure how big it is 
(and it’s not like we can measure it anytime, that’s called harassment)
Fast forward to today, and Newgrounds has several thousand users on the platform, several nostalgic series that keep people coming back, 
and much more being created
Some notable series include Krinkel’s “Madness Combat”, SrPelo’s “Spooky Month”, and, most recently, Speedoru’s “Punch Punch Forever”, 
among a handful of other important names 
(including Zone-Sama and Arin Hansen of Game Grumps fame)

Believe it or not, the website was going through a small recession after the 2010s began, 
mainly because content platforms like Youtube and social media took over, not to mention the iPhone boom
(If you use Newgrounds on your phone, I’m sorry for you, it must be so tiny to see those entries)
It seemed like Newgrounds would never recover, but then came a HUGE outlier that no one was expecting
You see, Newgrounds hosts these “Game Jams” every year, and one of these types of jams is known as “Ludum Dare” 
Basically, game makers have to work around the prompt and whatever game is the coolest/most enticing wins
During the late months of 2020, Ludum 47, with its concept of “Stuck in a Loop” , was going on
Ninjamuffin wanted to submit something for the competition (he had already been active on the site for 5 years prior to this game jam) 
and asked some friends/recommended people to help
It didn’t win the competition, but Friday Night Funkin’ is one of the most successful games to come out of that jam, and the most popular game on the platform

Friday Night Funkin’ was originally about a guy who had to rap-battle his girl’s dad in order to gain his trust and have s*x with her
But it expanded into so much more than, after seeing the immense support from the community and because they wanted to make it better
They then got famous voice-actor/animator SrPelo to voice the Spooky Kids and allow them to use the characters for Week 2 
The same can be said with Pico in Week 3, who was actually added to give content until the Mommy Mearest week would be completed
Week 6 was actually created in February for “Pixel Day”, an annual event on Newground where artists have to draw in a pixelated style, pretty self-explanatory
However, it wasn’t until Week 7 that the game started to “take off”, with the addition of Sergeant John Tankmen from the Tankmen series 
The game got so popular that on the day of the update, the Newgrounds website shut down due to too many users accessing the site at once, 
but not to worry, they optimized the site and it was back online in a few days
And then, fast-forward 3 years later, and we see the release of Weekend 1 (alongside the Erect remixes, of course), which adds Nene and Darnell, 
two significant figures in the “Pico’s School” series

Newgrounds also allowed the crew to find new people to help with the project, like moawling for the Week 6 visuals and IvanAlmightly for Darnell’s vocals
I have a feeling it also helped with the music producers as well, as some contributors, like tsunyoshi and thisiscub,  have their own Newgrounds pages

All this yapping is me saying that Newgrounds has had an incredibly big influence when this game was being made
Even today, there are still going to be updates for new characters from Newgrounds, like Ritz the Rat and Hank J. Wimbleton
Heck, even Tom Fulp himself is overlooking the project (alongside his video game business The Behemoth and working on Nightmare Cops)

Now, this was a long post, I know, but I’ll leave y’all with this
Newgrounds is full of creativity and inspiration to be found
It’s also full of edgy content and straight-up p*rn, but that’s only if you choose to find it
You, yes you, should make an account right now, if only to “favorite” or “blam” some content out the freakin’ window
If you want, you can even make Newgrounds the primary source of your content, whether it be audio or animation
The website is diverse and will allow for practically anything as long as it’s within TOS (but that’s less strict than other sites)
I believe that long after Youtube becomes a cesspool of MrBeast clones and branrot, 
Newgrounds will still be trekking on with users who want to make content they enjoy
I mean, it’s Everything by Everyone, what did you expect?

